          "path": "_m/g/c/m/n/penrhyn-quarry-wp/chwarel-y-penrhyn-from-y-fronl.jpg",
          "filename": "Chwarel y Penrhyn from Y Fronllwyd - geograph.org.uk - 219447.jpg",
          "caption": "Chwarel y Penrhyn from Y Fronllwyd.  This a view into the newly extended upper pit of Penrhyn Quarry from the slopes of Y Fronllwyd. Chwarel y Penrhyn, owned by McAlpines, is only major working slate quarry in Snowdonia and is highly mechanised. Today, its workforce is around 300, compared with 2889 in its labour intensive 1882 hey-day.",
