        {
          "path": "_m/g/c/m/n/penrhyn-quarry-wp/blasting-at-the-penrhyn-quarry.jpg",
          "filename": "Blasting at the Penrhyn Quarry viewed from Cwm Ffrydlas - geograph.org.uk - 432420.jpg",
          "caption": "Blasting at the Penrhyn Quarry viewed from Cwm Ffrydlas I had just started on my lunch when the 'take cover' siren was sounded at the Penrhyn. This was followed a minute or two later by a series of blasts and shortly afterwards by the warble of the 'all clear'. Today's firings are a tame affair compared with those of yesteryear when there would be simultaneous blasting on all the galleries, but it was enough to bring back memories of a time when you could set your watch by the twice daily blastings - always on the hour - from different quarries in the district.",
          "alt": "Blasting at the Penrhyn Quarry viewed from Cwm Ffrydlas I had just started on my lunch when the 'take cover' siren was sounded at the Penrhyn. This was followed a minute or two later by a series of blasts and shortly afterwards by the warble of the 'all clear'. Today's firings are a tame affair compared with those of yesteryear when there would be simultaneous blasting on all the galleries, but it was enough to bring back memories of a time when you could set your watch by the twice daily blastings - always on the hour - from different quarries in the district.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 480,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Eric Jones",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Blasting_at_the_Penrhyn_Quarry_viewed_from_Cwm_Ffrydlas_-_geograph.org.uk_-_432420.jpg",
